    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Symbotic Inc. is a public company headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts, and trades under the ticker SYM. Its website presents it as a provider of end-to-end warehouse automation for retailers and distributors, combining robotic systems with software. The company says its systems are intended to increase facility capacity through dense storage, raise throughput, and create efficiency gains across the supply chain, and that its solutions can be adapted to industries handling palletized goods, small quantity fulfillment, or omnichannel operations.\n\nThe company describes itself as the software and key robotic innovator behind each of its solutions, offering turnkey automation rather than relying on a portfolio of technology partnerships as it says typical integrators do. It states that goods as small as 1 lb (0.5 kg) and 2 x 6.4 x 5 in (5.1 x 16.3 x 12.7 cm) and as large as 60 lb (27.2 kg) and 36 x 24 x 16.2 in (91.4 x 61 x 41.2 cm) can be managed and fulfilled in their native packaging, with options for loose items and cold chain requirements. Symbotic describes itself as a leader in industrial automation and says it is pursuing AI software and robotics for material handling logistics.\n\nCorporate records list Symbotic as a for-profit public company with CIK 0001837240. Its litigation exposure is recorded in Massachusetts, with 176 cases.",
